{"id": "690359", "revid": "715442", "url": "https://vi.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=690359", "title": "Nervilia aragoana", "text": "Nervilia aragoana or the Tall Shield Orchid is small terrestrial orchid found in the McIlwraith Range in Queensland, Australia, from 0–150 metres altitude which flowers from September to December. It is also found in Ấn Độ, Malaysia, northern Thailand, Lào, Myanmar, Indonesia và New Guinea. North of the equator it blooms between January and April.\nVernacular names.\nMalaysia: Daun sa-helai sa-tahun, daun satu tahun (Peninsular).\nThailand: Phaen din yen (Chiang Rai), waan phra chim (Bangkok).\nVietnam: Ch[aa]n tr[aa]u xanh, thanh thi[ee]n q[uf]y, Ian c[owf].\nMiêu tả.\nLeaf appears kidney to heart-shaped, 150–250 mm. across, concave but with erect wavy edges. The flower stem is 200–250 mm. tall with 2-6 flowers."}
